# Run transcripts (notes.py) -- real target IPs, exploit techniques,
# captured flags. Same private-by-default posture as the vault's
# `Recon Output/*` (see the top-level .gitignore); this is the fallback
# location used when --target-name isn't given, so it needs its own rule.
runs/

# Third-party enumeration/exploit scripts the operator drops in for
# serve_payloads (linpeas.sh, winPEAS.exe, pspy64, ...) -- never bundled
# or committed here, both for licensing (GPL/PEASS-ng) and because they
# go stale independently of this harness. See README.md's Setup section.
payloads/

# Real secrets (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY etc.) -- see .env.example for the
# template and config.py's _load_dotenv() for how it's read.
.env

# Local Python virtualenv -- never bundle interpreter/deps, they're
# platform-specific and reproducible from a fresh `python -m venv` +
# `pip install`. Was missing until 2026-08-16 (found in the same pre-push
# gitignore audit as the top-level OffSec Labs//LLM Training/ gap) --
# 69MB that would have been swept into the repo on the next `git add .`.
.venv/
__pycache__/
